  "reason": "The current best (config_006, rna_only/multiprofile/scvi_n200/transformer, acc=0.653) establishes that multiprofile + scvi_n200 is the strongest RNA configuration. However, scgpt encoder is completely untested in the multiprofile setting, and in single-profile it has not been compared to scvi_n200. Testing config_009 (scgpt, multiprofile, transformer) directly isolates the encoder effect against the current best by changing only the RNA encoder. This is critical because the encoder choice determines the base representation for any subsequent multimodal fusion experiments; with only 4 experiments remaining, I need to confirm whether scgpt could surpass scvi_n200 before committing budget to multimodal configs built on a potentially suboptimal encoder. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, it opens a new promising branch; if not, I can confidently build multimodal experiments on the scvi_n200 base."
}

